# `fill_w` / `compress` are self-recursive tail loops that would
# benefit from #85 unroll, but their self-arm bodies have multiple
# pre-self statements (let bindings, side-effect rt-calls).  The
# detector currently requires arm_body.len() == 1, so unroll is a
# no-op on this workload until that's relaxed.  Tracked under #87
# follow-up.  Leave LAKE_UNROLL unset (= 1) for now.
